  "articleBody": "When you're planning a marble tile project, figuring out exactly how much to order can feel a bit like a guessing game. But it's actually super important to get it right! Just like with other natural stones, you'll want to order more than the exact square footage of your space. A good rule of thumb is to add about 10–15% to your total. This extra material accounts for a few things: cuts that need to be made, any accidental breakage during handling or installation, and a little bit for blending tiles to get that perfect veining pattern. Plus, having a few extra tiles on hand for future repairs is always a smart move. Imagine needing to replace a damaged tile years from now; having a match from the original lot will save you a lot of grief. Don't underestimate the power of those few extra pieces to ensure a smooth installation and long-term peace of mind. Chat with your installer, and they can help you nail down the perfect quantity for your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}